# A steel ball held under an electromagnet. The magnet is an IC-field: port 1 is
# the coil, storing flux linkage p1 with current p1*gap/K, and port 2 the gap,
# where it pulls with force p1^2/(2*K). Open loop this is unstable; the voltage
# source closes a PD loop on the gap, V = (the holding voltage at r) +
# k_p*(gap - r) + k_d*(gap rate), and r(t) steps the gap from 10 to 12 mm.
# Linearize it (about gap r, flux sqrt(2*K*m*g)) to see the loop's poles.

junction coil 1: V-, Rc+, Mag.1+
junction gap 1: Mag.2+, ball+, W-

element V Se value=R_c*sqrt(2*K*m*g)*r(t)/K+k_p*(q_Mag_2-r(t))+k_d*f_ball
element Rc R R=R_c
element Mag ICfield f1=p1*q2/K e2=p1^2/(2*K)
element ball I I=m
element W Se value=m*g

output gap_mm = 1000*q_Mag_2
output current = f_Rc
output voltage = e_V

# --- editor data (comments; bondgraph.py ignores these) ---
#@title Magnetic levitation with PD control (IC-field)
#@pos V 100 240
#@pos coil 280 240
#@pos Rc 280 100
#@pos Mag 470 240
#@pos gap 660 240
#@pos ball 660 100
#@pos W 840 240
#@param m=0.05
#@param g=9.81
#@param K=1e-3
#@param R_c=10
#@param k_p=390
#@param k_d=5.1
#@input r=0.01+0.002*Heaviside(t-0.3)
#@init q_Mag_2=0.01
#@init p_Mag=sqrt(2*K*m*g)
#@sim tEnd=1 steps=2000
